{"name":"Gran Torino Red","hex":"#ee3300","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gran","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A grandmother."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A grandfather. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gran"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gran Torino","blocks":[{"text":"Gran Torino is a 2008 drama film produced and directed by Clint Eastwood, who also stars in the lead role. The film features a significant Hmong American cast, a first for mainstream American films. Kyle Eastwood and Michael Stevens composed the score, while Jamie Cullum and Clint Eastwood provided the lead track."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c6/Gran_Torino_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gran_Torino","wikidata":"Q126699"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"},{"title":"Ford Torino","blocks":[{"text":"The Ford Torino is an automobile that was produced by Ford for the North American market between 1968 and 1976. It was a competitor in the intermediate market segment and essentially a twin to the Mercury Montego line."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/1970_ford_torino_cobra_sportsroof_chiolero.jpg/330px-1970_ford_torino_cobra_sportsroof_chiolero.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Torino","wikidata":"Q1361017"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c6/Gran_Torino_poster.jpg/250px-Gran_Torino_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c6/Gran_Torino_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c6/Gran_Torino_poster.jpg/250px-Gran_Torino_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGran_Torino_poster.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/St._Ambrose_Catholic_Church_-_Grosse_Pointe%2C_Michigan.jpg/500px-St._Ambrose_Catholic_Church_-_Grosse_Pointe%2C_Michigan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/St._Ambrose_Catholic_Church_-_Grosse_Pointe%2C_Michigan.jpg/1280px-St._Ambrose_Catholic_Church_-_Grosse_Pointe%2C_Michigan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.or